        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Woo, Epic Mazur, Park Jimin, Jae, Eazy-E, Bilal Bashir\n- Organizations: XING Entertainment, Ruthless Records, Relativity Records\n- Products: After School Club, Future Profits, \"Butterfly\"\n- Places: California, South Korea\n- Roles: singer, actor, television host, vocalist, rapper, record producer\n- Topics: music television, album production\n\nFacts:\n- Epic Mazur was born as Bret Hadley Mazur on August 31, 1970.\n- Future Profits was released on November 16, 1993 by Ruthless Records and Relativity Records.\n- Future Profits was produced by Eazy-E, Epic Mazur, and Bilal Bashir.\n- Kevin Woo was born as Christopher Thomas Woo on November 25, 1991.\n- Kevin Woo is an American singer, actor, and television host based in South Korea.\n- Kevin Woo was born and raised in California.\n- XING Entertainment discovered Kevin Woo when he was fifteen, and he then moved to South Korea.\n- Epic Mazur is an American vocalist, rapper, and record producer.\n- Epic Mazur is best known as a founder and frontman of Crazy Town and for the hit song \"Butterfly.\"\n- After School Club is a South Korean internet-based live-music request television talk show co-hosted by Kevin Woo, Park Jimin, and Jae.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
